From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:17:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(workflow): give condition outcomes a PersistentId

conditionOutcomeToGen() wrote Boolean, EnumerationValue and Void
condition outcomes without a PersistentId. Activities, UserTaskOutcome
and ParallelSplitOutcome all get one via addFreshPersistentID.

The runtime identifies an outcome an instance has taken by its
persistent ID, so an outcome stored without one is a new outcome on
every load. Every instance already past a decision (or past a
call-microflow task with outcomes) turned Incompatible on the next
deploy, a restart with no model change included: "A selected outcome
has been replaced in the already executed path".

Field-proven on v0.24.0 + this change, Mendix 11.13.0: a workflow
with 30 condition outcomes went from 0/30 to 30/30 carrying an ID,
mx check 0 errors; an instance paused at a user task after the
decisions stayed InProgress across a no-change restart and then ran
to Completed. Re-running create or replace workflow kept all 84 IDs
(CarryPersistentIDs), so the fix costs one re-ID on first write only.

